TTYCHATTER.BASH(1)          User Commands          TTYCHATTER.BASH(1)

NAME
    ttychatter.bash - dependency-light Bash-only terminal client

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter.bash [session]
    ttychatter.bash --resume <session|session.log|/path/session.log>
    ttychatter.bash --models
    ttychatter.bash --update-models
    ttychatter.bash --test-model <model_id>
    ttychatter.bash --select-model
    ttychatter.bash --doctor
    ttychatter.bash --demo
    ttychatter.bash --version
    ttychatter.bash --loopback
    ttychatter.bash --loopback-file <path>
    ttychatter.bash --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter.bash is the Bash-only edition of ttychatter. It avoids Python and
    remains dependency-light while still providing an end-user interactive chat
    client with sessions, model tools, memory, logs, and attachment attempts.

API KEYS
    API keys may be loaded from:
        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
        TTYCHATTER_API_KEY
        OPENROUTER_API_KEY or API_KEY in config
        API_KEY_GPG_FILE via external gpg decryption

    The default encrypted key file is:
        ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/api-key.gpg

    GPG support is optional. If gpg is missing or decryption fails, normal API
    key prompts/errors are used.

RUNTIME COMMAND MODE
    During interactive chat, inputs beginning with ':' are local commands rather
    than messages to OpenRouter. Examples:
        :help
        :models
        :select-model
        :test-model openrouter/auto
        :memory
        :attach ./notes.txt
        :credits
        :quit

LOOPBACK OUTPUT
    ttychatter.bash --loopback
        Runs the interactive chat normally, but sends prompts, status text,
        separators, and runtime-command output to stderr while clean AI
        responses are written to stdout. This allows the user to pipe AI
        responses into another program without mixing user-interface text into
        the pipe.

    ttychatter.bash --loopback-file <path>
        Appends each AI response to the named file while preserving the normal
        interactive display.

DEMO MODE
    --demo provides local model rows and local AI responses so the client can be
    tested without making OpenRouter chat requests.

VERSION
    ttychatter.bash version 0.10.0-bash-only
